{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1708340,
  "courseSlug": "learn-flutter-dart-to-build-ios-android-apps",
  "courseTitle": "Flutter & Dart - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37143772",
      "title": "Understanding Size Constraints",
      "lectureOrder": 139,
      "videoOrder": 127,
      "sourceHash": "244de859134a93f96d0174b1226ae639ac941fcb7542bcdb7cfdf6f0bd1d036c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.07,
          "end": 3.66,
          "en": "Now before we continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.66,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "with adjusting our app to different device sizes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.02,
          "end": 9.33,
          "en": "and we, for example, work on this modal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.33,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "and how it looks like in landscape mode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 14.913,
          "en": "there's one thing I want to take a closer look at.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.81,
          "end": 19.17,
          "en": "And that would be widget size constraints,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.17,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "or specifically the issue we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "with the chart not working inside of a Row.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 29.28,
          "en": "I want to make sure that you really understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.28,
          "end": 32.94,
          "en": "what exactly the problem was with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "and why we need Expanded here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 36.99,
          "en": "And for that it's really important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.99,
          "end": 40.5,
          "en": "to understand the concept of size constraints in Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.5,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "and to understand how in general Flutter widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 46.263,
          "en": "get sized and displayed on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.31,
          "end": 48.9,
          "en": "Because it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.9,
          "end": 51.3,
          "en": "that widgets actually get sized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.3,
          "end": 54.09,
          "en": "based on their size preferences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.09,
          "end": 58.83,
          "en": "and the size constraints applied by the parent widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.83,
          "end": 61.77,
          "en": "And to make this sentence a little bit less abstract,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.77,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "let's take a look at the Column widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "This Column widget has some preferences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.2,
          "en": "regarding the size it wants to occupy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.2,
          "end": 73.02,
          "en": "It wants to take as much height as it can get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.02,
          "end": 75,
          "en": "but it only needs as much width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "as defined by its largest child,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 80.223,
          "en": "So as defined by its children overall.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.51,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "But since the Column, in theory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 86.91,
          "en": "of course, wants to take as much height as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.91,
          "end": 90.81,
          "en": "it's important that the Column widget is inside of a parent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.81,
          "end": 93.36,
          "en": "that restricts the height because otherwise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.36,
          "end": 95.52000000000001,
          "en": "it would go outside of the screen boundaries,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 96.963,
          "en": "which is not the goal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 99.45,
          "en": "That's why we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.45,
          "end": 102.69,
          "en": "have no problem if a Column is used directly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.69,
          "end": 104.88,
          "en": "inside of a Scaffold widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.88,
          "end": 109.74000000000001,
          "en": "So as a value for the body parameter of a Scaffold widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.74000000000001,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "because the Scaffold widget turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 114.99000000000001,
          "en": "to constrain the height and the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.99000000000001,
          "end": 118.05,
          "en": "to the maximum device height or width.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.05,
          "end": 120.9,
          "en": "But every widget has different constraints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.9,
          "end": 122.31,
          "en": "for its child widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.31,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "So this is just an example here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "But for this example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 128.46,
          "en": "since we have the Column inside of a Scaffold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 130.2,
          "en": "with those constraints,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.2,
          "end": 133.44,
          "en": "the result would be that the maximum Column height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.44,
          "end": 135.78,
          "en": "is actually the maximum device height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.78,
          "end": 138.39,
          "en": "because that is the constraint by the parent widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.39,
          "end": 140.91,
          "en": "and the constraint of the parent widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 140.91,
          "end": 144.39,
          "en": "overwrites the preferences of the child widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "That's how sizing generally works in Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 149.97,
          "en": "And you can actually see this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.97,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "if you open the Flutter dev tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 154.563,
          "en": "Here, I'm doing this in a browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 155.46,
          "end": 157.26,
          "en": "Now if we open this Flutter inspector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 157.26,
          "end": 159.09,
          "en": "we can browse this widget tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 159.09,
          "end": 160.98,
          "en": "and select different widgets there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 160.98,
          "end": 163.35,
          "en": "And if we, for example, select this Column,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 163.35,
          "end": 166.23,
          "en": "which is right below the Scaffold,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 166.23,
          "end": 168.69,
          "en": "we can see that here on the right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 168.69,
          "end": 171.27,
          "en": "we get this layout explorer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 171.27,
          "end": 173.61,
          "en": "And this layout explorer, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 173.61,
          "end": 176.94,
          "en": "tells us the height and the width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.94,
          "end": 179.52,
          "en": "that was assigned to this Column widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.52,
          "end": 180.735,
          "en": "but it also tells us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 180.735,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "the constraints this Column widget get from its parent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 186.57,
          "en": "So in this case, from the Scaffold.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 186.57,
          "end": 187.71,
          "en": "And here, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 187.71,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "we see that for the width the constraint was that anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 194.55,
          "en": "between zero and the maximum device width is allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.55,
          "end": 199.023,
          "en": "And for the height it's the same, zero and maximum height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 201.45,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "And therefore the Column widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 206.94,
          "en": "actually chose the maximum height and the maximum width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 206.94,
          "end": 208.77,
          "en": "though the width simply depends",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 208.77,
          "end": 211.23,
          "en": "on the child widgets inside of the column.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 211.23,
          "end": 213.9,
          "en": "Because as mentioned before, for the Column widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.9,
          "end": 216.63,
          "en": "and actually for most Flutter widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 216.63,
          "end": 219.09,
          "en": "the actual height or width that is taken",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 219.09,
          "end": 221.553,
          "en": "depends on what the child widgets want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.54,
          "end": 225.39,
          "en": "Though for the Column widget, there is something special",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.39,
          "end": 227.55,
          "en": "to be noted regarding the height constraints",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 227.55,
          "end": 229.74,
          "en": "it passes down to its children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "So to the Chart, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 233.55,
          "en": "which is inside of the Column.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 233.55,
          "end": 236.67000000000002,
          "en": "We can see those constraints in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 236.67000000000002,
          "end": 240.06,
          "en": "Here we see that it's unconstrained vertically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 240.06,
          "end": 242.7,
          "en": "so that the Column widget does not pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 242.7,
          "end": 246.06,
          "en": "any height constraints to its child widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 246.06,
          "end": 249.06,
          "en": "so to the widgets that are passed to the Column.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 249.06,
          "end": 251.64,
          "en": "And that, for example, would be a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 251.64,
          "end": 252.64,
          "en": "for the ExpensesList",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 253.89,
          "end": 256.32,
          "en": "because this in the end renders a ListView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 256.32,
          "end": 260.79,
          "en": "which is also just a list and kind of a Column therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 260.79,
          "end": 262.8,
          "en": "And indeed the ListView",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 262.8,
          "end": 266.76,
          "en": "by default also would have no constraints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 266.76,
          "end": 269.79,
          "en": "We don't see it here when we select the ListView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 269.79,
          "end": 273.09000000000003,
          "en": "but actually if we select the child inside of the ListView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 273.09000000000003,
          "end": 274.8,
          "en": "this Dismissible widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 274.8,
          "end": 277.08,
          "en": "we can see that for the Dismissible widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 277.08,
          "end": 279.45,
          "en": "its height is unconstrained.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 279.45,
          "end": 281.19,
          "en": "And since it is inside of the ListView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 281.19,
          "end": 282.96,
          "en": "that of course means that it's the ListView",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 282.96,
          "end": 286.11,
          "en": "that's not constraining the height for Dismissible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 286.11,
          "end": 290.01,
          "en": "So ListView has a unconstrained height as does Column,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 290.01,
          "end": 292.68,
          "en": "and therefore ListView would not be restricted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 292.68,
          "end": 294.65999999999997,
          "en": "in the height it tries to take up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 294.65999999999997,
          "end": 297.57,
          "en": "And therefore it would of course go out of the boundaries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 297.57,
          "end": 300.63,
          "en": "of the device screen on which the app is running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 300.63,
          "end": 303.81,
          "en": "because there simply is no height constraint.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 303.81,
          "end": 307.17,
          "en": "And that's exactly why you need this Expanded wrapper here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 307.17,
          "end": 310.56,
          "en": "because Expanded does something special.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 310.56,
          "end": 313.59,
          "en": "If you add Expanded as we're doing it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 313.59,
          "end": 314.76,
          "en": "around the ListView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 314.76,
          "end": 319.29,
          "en": "in the end, Expanded does set height constraints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 319.29,
          "end": 322.29,
          "en": "It sets the maximum height of its child widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 322.29,
          "end": 325.71,
          "en": "so of the ListView in case of this Expanded widget here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 325.71,
          "end": 328.02,
          "en": "to the maximum available height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 328.02,
          "end": 330.42,
          "en": "Instead of getting as much height as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 330.42,
          "end": 332.7,
          "en": "so a height of infinity in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 332.7,
          "end": 335.34000000000003,
          "en": "it takes as much height as it can get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 335.34000000000003,
          "end": 336.87,
          "en": "And that's an important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 336.87,
          "end": 339.54,
          "en": "compared to an infinite amount of height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 339.54,
          "end": 343.35,
          "en": "which is what Column and ListView would set as constraints.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 343.35,
          "end": 345.45,
          "en": "Expanded narrows that down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 345.45,
          "end": 348.51,
          "en": "and limits the available height to its child widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 348.51,
          "end": 351.6,
          "en": "so to the ListView in case of this Expanded widget here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 351.6,
          "end": 354.15,
          "en": "to the actual available height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 354.15,
          "end": 357.87,
          "en": "that's why wrapping unconstrained widgets with Expanded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 357.87,
          "end": 360.36,
          "en": "makes sure that unconstrained widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 360.36,
          "end": 362.85,
          "en": "inside of other unconstrained widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 362.85,
          "end": 366.24,
          "en": "as we have it here with ListView inside of Column,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 366.24,
          "end": 368.76,
          "en": "doesn't cause any problems anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 368.76,
          "end": 372.84,
          "en": "That's also the problem we fixed here with the Row and Chart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 372.84,
          "end": 376.38,
          "en": "because Chart actually does not render a Row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 376.38,
          "end": 379.35,
          "en": "but a Container where I explicitly set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 379.35,
          "end": 382.11,
          "en": "the width to double.infinity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 382.11,
          "end": 384.45,
          "en": "to make sure that this container takes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 384.45,
          "end": 387.48,
          "en": "as much space as it can possibly get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 387.48,
          "end": 388.77,
          "en": "But of course that's a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 388.77,
          "end": 390.63,
          "en": "if we do this inside of a Row,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 390.63,
          "end": 393.093,
          "en": "which also has a width of infinity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 394.14,
          "end": 396.69,
          "en": "With Expanded, as I just described,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 396.69,
          "end": 400.05,
          "en": "this is fixed because expanded between Row and Chart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 400.05,
          "end": 402.63,
          "en": "makes sure that chart is actually limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 402.63,
          "end": 406.77,
          "en": "and can only take as much width as is actually available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 406.77,
          "end": 408.87,
          "en": "And that's how widgets are sized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 408.87,
          "end": 411.96,
          "en": "and what size constraints are all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 411.96,
          "end": 414.51,
          "en": "This in the end, explains why certain widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 414.51,
          "end": 417.69,
          "en": "can be used inside of other widgets without problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 417.69,
          "end": 420.12,
          "en": "and why, for example, a Column inside of a Column",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 420.12,
          "end": 421.23,
          "en": "could cause a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 421.23,
          "end": 424.35,
          "en": "but those problems then can be fixed, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 424.35,
          "end": 427.233,
          "en": "by adding an Expanded widget between the two Columns.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
